<concept id="t00280">
	<title id="e02103">Current trip</title>
	<conbody>
		<table frame="none" colsep="1" rowsep="1" outputclass="formatc_none" id="e02104">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1" outputclass="formatc">
				<colspec colnum="1" colname="1" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colnum="2" colname="2" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="0">
						<entry colname="1" colsep="0">
							<fig id="e02105">
								<figgroup>
									<image align="center" height="1.575in" href="../../images/OOV035119L.eps" placement="break" width="2.244in" id="e02106"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry>
							<ol outputclass="callout" id="e02107">
								<li>
									<p> <uicontrol>Current Trip Info</uicontrol> </p>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p> <uicontrol>Trip</uicontrol> </p>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p> <uicontrol>Timer</uicontrol> </p>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p> <uicontrol>Avg.</uicontrol> </p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<ul id="e02108">
			<li id="e02109">
				<p>The trip computer mode displays information related to vehicle driving parameters including average energy consumption, tripmeter information, and vehicle speed.</p>
			</li>
			<li id="e02110">
				<p>Turn off the vehicle and open the driver’s seat door or turn on the vehicle 3 minutes after turning it off, and the Current trip is automatically initialized.</p>
			</li>
			<li id="e02111">
				<p>If the vehicle is running, even when the vehicle is not in motion, the information will be accumulated.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</conbody>
</concept>